  <text>
    <body>
      <div>
        <head>In the directories</head>
        <p>R. G. McMullen is listed at No. 47 <ref target="civic?id=Madeline%20Street">Madeline Street</ref> in 1900 and 1905, as a labour agent in 1905.</p>
      </div>
      <div>
        <head>On the electoral roll</head>
        <p>Richard McMullen, agent, is on the 1905 <ref target="civic?id=Electoral-Rolls">electoral roll</ref> at 47 Madeline Street, with Ellen McMullen, home duties.</p>
      </div>
      <div>
        <head>Neighbours</head>
        <p>The grocer <ref target="civic?id=William%20Norris">William Norris</ref> is next door at No. 45. On the other side, C. Dargie, engineer and costume stand maker, is at No. 49 in 1900, and <ref target="civic?id=Carl%20Fischer">Carl Fischer</ref>, hairdresser and tobacconist, in 1905.</p>
      </div>
